---The settings for the source of the flow.
---@class aws.mediaconnect.SetSourceRequest
---@field Decryption? aws.mediaconnect.Encryption The type of encryption that is used on the content ingested from this source. Allowable encryption types: static-key.
---@field Description? string A description for the source. This value is not used or seen outside of the current MediaConnect account.
---@field EntitlementArn? string The ARN of the entitlement that allows you to subscribe to this flow. The entitlement is set by the flow originator, and the ARN is generated as part of the originator's flow.
---@field IngestPort? number The port that the flow will be listening on for incoming content.
---@field MaxBitrate? number The smoothing max bitrate (in bps) for RIST, RTP, and RTP-FEC streams.
---@field MaxLatency? number The maximum latency in milliseconds. This parameter applies only to RIST-based and Zixi-based streams.
---@field MaxSyncBuffer? number The size of the buffer (in milliseconds) to use to sync incoming source data.
---@field MediaStreamSourceConfigurations? aws.mediaconnect.__listOfMediaStreamSourceConfigurationRequest The media streams that are associated with the source, and the parameters for those associations.
---@field MinLatency? number The minimum latency in milliseconds for SRT-based streams. In streams that use the SRT protocol, this value that you set on your MediaConnect source or output represents the minimal potential latency of that connection. The latency of the stream is set to the highest number between the sender’s minimum latency and the receiver’s minimum latency.
---@field Name? string The name of the source.
---@field Protocol? aws.mediaconnect.Protocol|string The protocol that is used by the source.
---@field SenderControlPort? number The port that the flow uses to send outbound requests to initiate connection with the sender.
---@field SenderIpAddress? string The IP address that the flow communicates with to initiate connection with the sender.
---@field SourceListenerAddress? string Source IP or domain name for SRT-caller protocol.
---@field SourceListenerPort? number Source port for SRT-caller protocol.
---@field StreamId? string The stream ID that you want to use for this transport. This parameter applies only to Zixi and SRT caller-based streams.
---@field VpcInterfaceName? string The name of the VPC interface to use for this source.
---@field WhitelistCidr? string The range of IP addresses that should be allowed to contribute content to your source. These IP addresses should be in the form of a Classless Inter-Domain Routing (CIDR) block; for example, 10.0.0.0/16.
---@field GatewayBridgeSource? aws.mediaconnect.SetGatewayBridgeSourceRequest The source configuration for cloud flows receiving a stream from a bridge.
---@field NdiSourceSettings? aws.mediaconnect.NdiSourceSettings The settings for the NDI® source. This includes the exact name of the upstream NDI sender that you want to connect to your source.
---@field SourceTags? aws.mediaconnect.__mapOfString The key-value pairs that can be used to tag and organize the source.
---@field RouterIntegrationState? aws.mediaconnect.State|string Indicates whether to enable or disable router integration when setting a flow source.
---@field RouterIntegrationTransitDecryption? aws.mediaconnect.FlowTransitEncryption The decryption configuration for the flow source when router integration is enabled. Specifies how the source content should be decrypted when router integration is used.
---@field RtmpPushSettings? aws.mediaconnect.SetRtmpPushSourceSettings The settings for the RTMP (Real-Time Messaging Protocol) source.

