---@field SenderControlPort? number The port that the flow uses to send outbound requests to initiate connection with the sender.
---@field SenderIpAddress? string The IP address that the flow communicates with to initiate connection with the sender.
---@field SmoothingLatency? number The smoothing latency in milliseconds for RIST, RTP, and RTP-FEC streams.
---@field SourceListenerAddress? string Source IP or domain name for SRT-caller protocol.
---@field SourceListenerPort? number Source port for SRT-caller protocol.
---@field StreamId? string The stream ID that you want to use for this transport. This parameter applies only to Zixi and SRT caller-based streams.
---@field NdiSpeedHqQuality? number A quality setting for the NDI Speed HQ encoder.
---@field NdiProgramName? string A suffix for the name of the NDI® sender that the flow creates. If a custom name isn't specified, MediaConnect uses the output name.
---@field NdiSourceSettings? aws.mediaconnect.NdiSourceSettings The settings for the NDI source. This includes the exact name of the upstream NDI sender that you want to connect to your source.
---@field NdiOutputTimecodeSource? aws.mediaconnect.NdiOutputTimecodeSource The timecode source for NDI output frames. For NDI outputs, this field is always present and defaults to EMBEDDED_TIMECODE.
---@field NdiAudioReferenceLevel? aws.mediaconnect.NdiAudioReferenceLevel The audio reference level of the NDI receiver, in decibels relative to full scale (dBFS). Common values are -20 (NDI and SMPTE) and -18 (EBU). For NDI outputs, this field is always present and defaults to -20.
---@field RtmpPushSourceSettings? aws.mediaconnect.RtmpPushSourceSettings The settings for the RTMP (Real-Time Messaging Protocol) source.
---@field RtmpPushOutputSettings? aws.mediaconnect.RtmpPushOutputSettings The settings for an output that pushes a stream to a destination using the RTMP (Real-Time Messaging Protocol) protocol, or RTMPS (RTMP over TLS) when TLS encryption is specified.

