---Information about the encryption of the flow.
---@class aws.mediaconnect.UpdateEncryption
---@field Algorithm? aws.mediaconnect.Algorithm|string The type of algorithm that is used for the encryption (such as aes128, aes192, or aes256).
---@field ConstantInitializationVector? string A 128-bit, 16-byte hex value represented by a 32-character string, to be used with the key for encrypting content. This parameter is not valid for static key encryption.
---@field DeviceId? string The value of one of the devices that you configured with your digital rights management (DRM) platform key provider. This parameter is required for SPEKE encryption and is not valid for static key encryption.
---@field KeyType? aws.mediaconnect.KeyType|string The type of key that is used for the encryption. If no keyType is provided, the service will use the default setting (static-key).
---@field Region? string The Amazon Web Services Region that the API Gateway proxy endpoint was created in. This parameter is required for SPEKE encryption and is not valid for static key encryption.
---@field ResourceId? string An identifier for the content. The service sends this value to the key server to identify the current endpoint. The resource ID is also known as the content ID. This parameter is required for SPEKE encryption and is not valid for static key encryption.
---@field RoleArn? string The ARN of the role that you created during setup (when you set up MediaConnect as a trusted entity).
---@field SecretArn? string The ARN of the secret that you created in Secrets Manager to store the encryption key. This parameter is required for static key encryption and is not valid for SPEKE encryption.
---@field Url? string The URL from the API Gateway proxy that you set up to talk to your key server. This parameter is required for SPEKE encryption and is not valid for static key encryption.

---The settings for source failover.
---@class aws.mediaconnect.UpdateFailoverConfig
---@field FailoverMode? aws.mediaconnect.FailoverMode|string The type of failover you choose for this flow. MERGE combines the source streams into a single stream, allowing graceful recovery from any single-source loss. FAILOVER allows switching between different streams.
---@field RecoveryWindow? number Recovery window time to look for dash-7 packets.
---@field SourcePriority? aws.mediaconnect.SourcePriority The priority you want to assign to a source. You can have a primary stream and a backup stream or two equally prioritized streams.
---@field State? aws.mediaconnect.State|string The state of source failover on the flow. If the state is inactive, the flow can have only one source. If the state is active, the flow can have one or two sources.

